","To calculate the time required to deliver the loading dose, we first need to convert the mass of the child from pounds to kilograms. Then, we can calculate the total loading dose and the time taken to inject the dose.

1. **Convert pounds to kilograms:**
   \[
   32 \text{ lb} \times \frac{1 \text{ kg}}{3.271 \text{ lb}} = 9.81 \text{ kg}
   \]

2. **Calculate the loading dose:**
   \[
   9.81 \text{ kg} \times 20 \text{ mg/kg} = 196.2 \text{ mg}
   \]

3. **Calculate the time taken to infuse the dose:**
   \[
   \frac{196.2 \text{ mg}}{0.5 \text{ mg/min}} = 392.4 \text{ min}
   \]

