","To find the mass of sodium fluoride in a 10 mL dose of Pic-Flu-Red Reaker, we use the given concentration:

0.044% (w/v) means 0.044 grams of sodium fluoride per 100 mL of solution.

To find the mass of sodium fluoride in 10 mL, we can set up a proportion:

\[
\frac{0.044 \text{ g}}{100 \text{ mL}} = \frac{x \text{ g}}{10 \text{ mL}}
\]

Solving for \(x\):

\[
x = \frac{0.044 \times 10}{100} = 0.0044 \text{ g}
\]

Now, we need to convert grams to milligrams:

\[
0.0044 \text{ g} \times 1000 \text{ mg/g} = 4.4 \text{ mg}
\]

