Calculate the entropy change (J/mol K) of the given reaction. The molar entropies [J/K mol] are given in brackets after each substance.

\[ 2 \text{PbS(s)} [91.2] + 3 \text{O}_2(g) [205.1] \rightarrow 2 \text{PbO(s)} [66.5] + 2 \text{SO}_2(g) [248.2] \]
</USER_REQUEST>

<ASSISTANT_RESPONSE>
The entropy change (\(\Delta S\)) for a reaction is calculated using the formula:

\[
\Delta S = \sum \Delta S_{\text{products}} - \sum \Delta S_{\text{reactants}}
\]

Substituting the given molar entropies:

\[
\Delta S = \left(2 \times 66.5 + 2 \times 248.2\right) - \left(2 \times 91.2 + 3 \times 205.1\right)
\]

\[
\Delta S = (133 + 496.4) - (182.4 + 615.3)
\]

\[
\Delta S = 629.4 - 797.7
\]

\[
\Delta S = -168.3 \text{ J/mol K}
\]

Thus, the entropy change for the reaction is \(\boxed{-168.3 \text{ J/mol K}}\).
</ASSISTANT_RESPONSE>

