C2H4O2 + 5O2 → 2CO2 + 2H2O

The standard enthalpy change for this reaction can be calculated as:

ΔHcomb(CH3COOH) = -2(ΔHc(CO2)) - 2(ΔHc(H2O)) + 1(ΔHc(C2H4O2))

