\[
\frac{1}{L_m} = \frac{1}{L_1} + \frac{1}{L_2}
\]  
where \( L_m \) is the flillability limit of the mixture, \( L_1 \) and \( L_2 \) are the flillability limits of the two components in the mixture.  

This equation is derived from the ideal gas law and assumes ideal mixing behavior.  

\boxed{
\begin{aligned}
&\text{The relationship used to estimate the flillability limits of mixtures from the data for individual fuels is:} \\
