\[
\frac{n!}{n_1! n_2!} \left( \frac{1}{2} \right)^n,
\]
where \( n \) is the total number of flips (12), and \( n_1 \) and \( n_2 \) are the number of heads and non-hands (respectively), respectively.

1. 9 heads:
\[
\frac{12!}{9!3!} \left( \frac{1}{2} \right)^{12} = \frac{12 \times 11 \times 10}{3 \times 2 \times 1} \left( \frac{1}{2} \right)^{12} = 1120 \left( \frac{1}{2} \right)^{12}
\]
