Time for B to catch up with A = Distance A has traveled / Relative speed of B with respect to A
Time for B to catch up with A = 30 km / 10 kmph = 3 hours

Now, we can calculate the distance from the start where B catches up with A.

Distance from start = B's speed * Time for B to catch up with A
Distance from start = 20 kmph * 3 hours = 60 km

