ΔG° = [2 × ΔG°f(H2O)] - [2 × ΔG°f(H2O) + 1 × ΔG°f(O2)]

Since the standard Gibbs free energy of formation for H2 and O2 is 0 kJ/mol, we can simplify the equation to:

ΔG° = 2 × (-237.1 kJ/mol) - 0 = -474.2 kJ/mol

