The balanced chemical equation for the reaction is:

2H2(g) + O2(g) → 2H2O(g)

The standard Gibbs free energy of formation (ΔG°f) for water (H2O) is -237.1 kJ/mol. We can use this value to find the standard Gibbs free energy change for the reaction:

ΔG° = [2 × ΔG°f(H2O)] - [2 × ΔG°f(H2O) + 1 × ΔG°f(O2)]

