","The coefficient of restitution \( e \) is defined as the ratio of the relative velocity of collision to the relative velocity of exit. The velocity of collision is \( v_1 \) and the velocity of ejection is \( v_2 \). The velocity of the wall is zero. Thus:
\[
e = \frac{v_2 - 0}{0 - v_1} = \frac{v_2}{v_1}
\]
Given \( e = \frac{1}{3} \), we have:
\[
\frac{v_2}{v_1} = \frac{1}{3} \implies v_2 = \frac{1}{3} v_1
\]
The velocity of the ball is along the horizontal direction, so the horizontal velocity is conserved. The horizontal velocity is \( v_1 \). After the collision, the horizontal velocity is \( v_2 \cos \theta \), where \( \theta \) is the angle of incidence. Since the ball rebounds at the same angle of incidence, the angle of exit is \( \theta \). Thus:
\[
v_1 = v_2 \cos \theta
\]
Substituting \( v_2 = \frac{1}{3} v_1 \):
\[
